## ⚠️ Security Warnings

### **NEVER Allow These Patterns:**
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Arbitrary email sending
export async function sendEmailToAnyone(email: string) {
  await sendEmail(email, "spam"); // NO!
}

// ❌ BAD: No authentication check
export async function updateOrder(orderId: string) {
  // Missing: const user = await getCurrentUser();
  await updateOrderInDB(orderId);
}

// ❌ BAD: Trust user input without validation
export async function processEmailJob(data: any) {
  await sendEmail(data.email, data.content); // NO!
}
```

### **ALWAYS Follow These Patterns:**
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Authentication required
export async function updateOrder(data: UpdateOrderData) {
  const user = await getCurrentUser();
  if (!user) return { error: "Authentication required" };
  
  // Check ownership before proceeding
}

// ✅ GOOD: Validate and sanitize
export async function processEmailJob(rawData: unknown) {
  const data = emailJobSchema.parse(rawData);
  await sendValidatedEmail(data);
}

// ✅ GOOD: User context maintained
export async function createOrder(data: OrderData) {
  const user = await getCurrentUser();
  const order = await createOrderWithUser(user.id, data);
  await queueOrderEmail(user.id, order); // User context preserved
}
```

This security implementation ensures that **only authenticated users can trigger emails for their own orders/accounts** and prevents any unauthorized email sending! 🛡️